CHECK bb27.1 TRUE with Auto.linpreds = FALSE the queue grows by two entries after a step that lists one term, the fit uses one more term than dirs shows (8 against 7), and the rank fix removes it
CHECK bb27.2 TRUE with Auto.linpreds = TRUE on the same data the queue sizes equal the visible term counts and no rank fix is printed
CHECK bb27.3 FALSE HYPOTHESIS over parts A, B and D, a linear-option step adds a hidden queue entry exactly when Auto.linpreds = FALSE and the parent is not the intercept (267 linear-option steps)
CHECK bb27.4 TRUE the rank fix appears only with Auto.linpreds = FALSE (46 of 80 such fits, and 0 of 80 with TRUE)
CHECK bb27.5 TRUE the forward pass computes GRSq with the visible terms only; the hidden term does not count
CHECK bb27.6 TRUE with Auto.linpreds = FALSE the kind of parent does not decide the hidden entry: in part D the first step, a linear-option step with the intercept as parent, adds one at degree 1 and 2 (design D1), while in part A the linear-option step at K = 10, with parent slot 2, adds none; only linear-option steps add one (0 of 942 other steps), and none with Auto.linpreds = TRUE
CHECK bb27.7 TRUE the column order changes it: on the same data (design D2), the first step takes the linear option on z with the intercept as parent, and adds a hidden entry when z is the last column but not when z is the first, at degree 1 and 2
CHECK bb27.8 TRUE in each of the 174 fits of parts A, B and D, earth prints the rank fix exactly when a step added a hidden entry, and the fit then uses as many more terms than dirs shows as there are hidden entries
